course: dictionary
lesson: 1389
title: Captivity: kept by people, not free
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Captivity means being kept in a place and not being free. A lion in a zoo is in captivity; a bird flying over a forest is not. Look for clues in the sentence: «Some people think keeping wild animals in captivity is wrong even with good care.» The words even with good care tell you that captivity is a state that can happen even when the animal is treated kindly.
explain: Captivity is uncountable, so we say "in captivity" or "bred in captivity", not "a captivity". «Blu in the film Rio is a Spix's macaw; birds bred in captivity were reported released in Brazil from 2022.» Bred in captivity means born and raised by people, not in the wild.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Elephants were never truly tamed; most were caught wild, as they breed slowly in captivity.» If you swap in "kept by people", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right. Captivity can also describe a prisoner held in a cell, as in history and stories.
fact: Captivity means the state of being kept in a place and not being free.
fact: «In captivity» means kept by people instead of living in the wild.
fact: «Bred in captivity» means born and raised by people, such as the platypus bred in captivity at Healesville Sanctuary in 1943.
fact: Zoos, sanctuaries and farms are places where animals may be kept in captivity, and prisoners are held in captivity too.
fact: The opposite of captivity is being free, and animals that live freely are said to live in the wild.
exercise: «Healesville Sanctuary bred the first platypus in captivity in 1943.» What does in captivity mean here? | *Kept by people instead of living in the wild | Sleeping in a warm nest | Swimming free in a river | Hidden under the ground
exercise: Which animal is most likely to be in captivity? | *A lion in a zoo | A bird singing in a tall gum tree | A fish swimming in the open sea | A kangaroo hopping across a wide plain
exercise: Tom says, «Captivity is a happy word, it means a holiday.» Is Tom right? | *No, it means being kept in a place and not being free | Yes, it means a happy holiday | Yes, it means a big party | No, it means a wild forest
test: «Leave wild frogs and tadpoles in their home; they usually die in captivity.» What does in captivity mean? | *Kept by people, away from their home, and not free | Living freely in a pond | Asleep under a stone | Kept by people, away from their home
test: «Elephants breed slowly in captivity.» Which meaning fits captivity best? | A big garden for picnics | Being wild and free | A sunny day at the beach | *Being kept by people and not free
exam: Which sentence uses captivity correctly? | *A bird bred in captivity was later released back into the wild | Captivity is a sunny beach where you can swim | The sky is in captivity above the clouds | Captivity means a big garden for picnics
